      "evidence_sha256": "cc729a4729bac394e7af2408252381b2c28a2d012f24491aa4fdf571efd5967f",
      "assessment": "R4 G4 performs a useful matched step75 current-geometry comparison after checking delivery, showing about20% lower mid-window motion and tiny geometry changes. But it samples the first five IDs without relevance-based selection, borrows the incumbent median for the last action, misstates a 0.00028 maximum geometry change as <=0.0002 and rewrites early tick5 Mean as4.060 rather than4.069.",
      "decision_update": "Both late bracket proposals [6,6,4,5] and [6,6,4,7] execute as R5 G3 and G4. They constitute a new conditional bracket, though the claim that earlier late evidence was only multi-component is false. This is a bounded useful test despite imperfect provenance.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Five arbitrary molecules cannot establish whole-population geometry insensitivity or explain the affinity contributors. It again supplies a 0.05/1e-4 decision band without uncertainty evidence and incorrectly describes the pending R5 proposals as if no sampling remained at R4.",
