    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r04/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "3db5142e88742570a7836576e26eea21b1f86d35d719c4b644be9ade597c4c7f",
      "assessment": "R4 synthesis identifies exact repeated arrays but selects two of them as safe final exploitation, plus the novel late bracket. It propagates the false 99-pairs quantile claim and dismisses a -0.015715 conditional Mean loss as no direction response. It uses statistically tied and noise language despite explicitly lacking an uncertainty estimate.",
      "decision_update": "R5 executes [6,5,6,5], [6,5,6,4], [6,6,4,5], [6,6,4,7]. The two repeated groups add no independent replication; the late bracket yields small effects. With one round left, ranking should trade verified expected Mean contribution against truly new conditional information, not automatically allocate repeats because they look safe.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The council cannot know whether unselected component/interaction probes would beat repeats. Low information value is an efficiency concern, not proof of an attainable better affinity. Existing retention already preserves best results, reducing the incremental output value of deterministic replay.",
