      "evidence_sha256": "66ddf53cf975ee046465d980519673d211428679b39b4f10e19d64c73815cdb4",
      "assessment": "R5 G1 accurately records restoration of the index1-down loss and distinguishes fixed schedule and composite benchmark. It preserves no-new-geometry and no-variance limitations. But it still calls the repeated -0.015715 loss an artifact rather than a real conditional Mean response and understates the spread among its listed top arms.",
      "decision_update": "Review-only proposals [6,5,5,5] and [6,6,6,5] are both selected into the final archived ranking; no R6 is executed. The latter explicitly tests index1-by-index2 context, a useful general hypothesis form that should be considered earlier when a remaining experiment can change decisions.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "There is no measured score for either final proposal in this context. Reproducing a concentrated loss on restoration is evidence about those candidates, not evidence of a broad population slope or a reason to ignore Mean.",
