    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r05/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "0aa0d133b502d8c5dfc7d11da0999c7cc45c40b3461d8d6f072f4ff6f545c691",
      "assessment": "R5 G2 keeps comparison directions, private-history labels and review-only status clear, and distinguishes inherited diagnostics from newly queried facts. It nevertheless repeats the false 99-pairs-within-quantile-band claim and requires broad/median movement to reject inertness, excluding genuine concentrated Mean response.",
      "decision_update": "[6,5,5,4] and [6,4,6,4] remain unselected and unexecuted. The latter is a recurrence/conditional-context hypothesis, which should specify contributor identities and observed quality if later pursued, rather than treating a same-candidate loss as no schedule effect.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Only summaries and incumbent pairing are fresh. Public memory is not a substitute for candidate traces; an inherited number should retain its original denominator, scope and uncertainty.",
